:0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.6.1.stable, 4.6.3.stable, 4.7.stable.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.stable - Windows 11\n\n### Issue description\n\nI noticed that if you mark an instantiated scene's exported resource as unique, then switch to editing that scene and save it (no actual edits needed), the inspector will show that resource as non-unique again. The resource seems to stay unique however, so this is only a visual bug. Interestingly, the shared resource indicator also says that \"This Resource is used in 2 places\" instead of the expected \"This resource is external to scene\". \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open linked MRP.\n2. Open main_scene.tscn, and select the ChildScene from the scene tree. The exported resource is shown as unique.\n3. Open child_scene.tscn, and save it.\n4. Switch back to main_scene.tscn. The exported resource is shown as non-unique, and can be made unique again.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[resource-bug-test_2026-06-23_19-12-02.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29258454/resource-bug-test_2026-06-23_19-12-02.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_